A git source in uv.lock must reach pip as `name @ git+url@rev`, not as `name==version`

MEASURED in mtools 2026-09-20 (rules_python 2.3.3, `pip.parse(uv_lock = ...)`): a dev group
carrying `paperkit` from `source = { git = "https://github.com/mikemol/paperkit#<sha>" }`
fails to fetch —

    ERROR: No matching distribution found for paperkit==0.1.0

`_parse_uv_lock_json` recognises the git source and builds a `git_struct` with `kind = "git"`,
then (a) emits `requirement_line = "{name}=={version}"` regardless of kind, and (b) carries
the git URL in `url`, so `hub_builder.bzl:649` skips the pip-installed fallback (`if not
src.url`) and hands the URL to bazel's downloader, which fetches the repository's HTML page
as a file named `paperkit`. pip is then asked for `paperkit==0.1.0` from `--find-links .`.

The form `uv pip compile` writes for the same lock — `paperkit @ git+https://…@<sha>` — is
what pip honours natively. So: for a git source, emit that line and leave `url` empty, which
routes the package through the pip path that already builds sdists. The revision fragment
uv.lock records after `#` is the resolved commit; a `?rev=` query is dropped because the
fragment supersedes it.

Applied by mtools' MODULE.bazel via single_version_override until upstream carries it.

--- a/python/private/pypi/parse_requirements.bzl
+++ b/python/private/pypi/parse_requirements.bzl
@@ -232,12 +232,20 @@
             url_path, _, _ = url.partition("?")
             url_path, _, _ = url_path.partition("#")
             _, _, filename = url_path.rpartition("/")
+            # pip's direct-reference form: `git+<url>@<rev>`. uv.lock records the resolved
+            # commit as the URL fragment; a `?rev=` query, when present, is the request the
+            # fragment answers, so it is dropped rather than duplicated.
+            _, _, rev = url.partition("#")
+            pip_url = "git+" + url_path + ("@" + rev if rev else "")
             git_struct = struct(
                 filename = filename,
-                url = url,
+                # Empty so hub_builder takes the pip-installed path: bazel's downloader cannot
+                # fetch a git repository and pip can.
+                url = "",
                 digest = "",
                 kind = "git",
                 source = pkg["source"],
+                pip_url = pip_url,
             )

         plat_to_src = {}
@@ -275,11 +283,20 @@
         for key, val in src_to_plats.items():
             src = val.src
             plats = sorted(val.plats)
-            requirement_line = "{name}{extras}=={version}".format(
-                name = name,
-                extras = extra_str,
-                version = version,
-            )
+            if getattr(src, "kind", None) == "git":
+                # A git source has no index version to ask for; pip resolves the
+                # direct reference itself.
+                requirement_line = "{name}{extras} @ {url}".format(
+                    name = name,
+                    extras = extra_str,
+                    url = src.pip_url,
+                )
+            else:
+                requirement_line = "{name}{extras}=={version}".format(
+                    name = name,
+                    extras = extra_str,
+                    version = version,
+                )
             entry["resolved_srcs"].append(struct(
                 distribution = name,
                 extra_pip_args = extra_pip_args or [],
